# Pairs with ReconcileDeletesOnlyDeleted. A range-scoped export (the anti-entropy
# bootstrap fallback's) carries nothing outside its ranges; reconciling there
# fabricates a delete of every source-origin key outside them, which s still holds.
MODULE: ReconcileDeletesOnlyDeletedOutOfScope
TARGET: ReconcileDeletesOnlyDeleted
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the reconcile ignores the export's scope, so a range-scoped export deletes keys it never covered
PERTURBS: EndExport

--- FIND
           orphan == ex.scope /\ ex.precap.present /\ ~ex.carried
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: scope is not consulted.
           orphan == ex.precap.present /\ ~ex.carried
--- END
